# Normalise line endings on checkout.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone (core.autocrlf=true) checks text files out with
# CRLF, and Docker's build context copies that working tree into the image.
# docker-entrypoint.sh then has a `#!/bin/sh\r` shebang and the container dies
# at startup with "exec /usr/local/bin/docker-entrypoint.sh: no such file or
# directory" — the image builds fine and then refuses to run.
#
# All blobs are already stored as LF, so this changes how files are checked
# out, not what is committed: no content churn in the repository.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never mangle binaries.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
